0,"Chilisso language - Simple English Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia",https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chilisso_language,Chilisso is an Indo-European Kohistani language spoken in Pakistan. It is also called Galos or Chiliss.,Chilisso,Indo-European
1,Chilisso | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/clh/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..2JlGzaieKQCQQEO-N8F3VU5y_wvAT54tsYFLtaEltqU,"Chilisso is an endangered indigenous language of Pakistan. It belongs to the Indo-European language family. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by a decreasing number of young people.",Chilisso,Indo-European
2,Chilisso language Facts for Kids,https://kids.kiddle.co/Chilisso_language,"Chilisso is a unique language that belongs to the Indo-European family. This means it shares ancient roots with many languages spoken across Europe and parts of Asia. It's a spoken language, meaning people use it to communicate every day.",Chilisso,Indo-European
